{"name":"Limousine Leather","hex":"#3b3c3b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"limousine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An automobile body with seats and permanent top like a coupe, and with the top projecting over the driver and a projecting front.","An automobile with such a body. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/limousine"},{"term":"leather","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tough material produced from the skin of animals, by tanning or similar process, used e.g. for clothing; often denotes leather from cattle when no qualifier specifies otherwise.","A piece of the above used for polishing."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of leather.","Referring to one who wears leather clothing (motorcycle jacket, chaps over 501 jeans, boots), especially as a sign of sadomasochistic homosexuality."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leather"}],"entries":[{"title":"Limousine","blocks":[{"text":"A limousine, or limo for short, is a large, chauffeur-driven luxury vehicle with a partition between the driver compartment and the passenger compartment which can be operated mechanically by hand or by a button electronically. A luxury sedan with a very long wheelbase and driven by a professional driver is called a stretch limousine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/1908StudeLimo.jpg/330px-1908StudeLimo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limousine","wikidata":"Q188475"},{"title":"Leather","blocks":[{"text":"Leather is a strong, flexible and durable material obtained from the tanning, or chemical treatment, of animal skins and hides to prevent decay. The most common leathers come from cattle, sheep, goats, equine animals, buffalo, pigs and hogs, ostriches, and aquatic animals such as seals and alligators."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Leathertools.jpg/330px-Leathertools.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leather","wikidata":"Q286"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Phantom_IV.jpg/330px-Phantom_IV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Phantom_IV.jpg/330px-Phantom_IV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhantom_IV.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/2013_Jaguar_Eagle_Limousine_V6_Diesel_Automatic_3.0.jpg/500px-2013_Jaguar_Eagle_Limousine_V6_Diesel_Automatic_3.0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/2013_Jaguar_Eagle_Limousine_V6_Diesel_Automatic_3.0.jpg/1280px-2013_Jaguar_Eagle_Limousine_V6_Diesel_Automatic_3.0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/2013_Jaguar_Eagle_Limousine_V6_Diesel_Automatic_3.0.jpg/500px-2013_Jaguar_Eagle_Limousine_V6_Diesel_Automatic_3.0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2013_Jaguar_Eagle_Limousine_V6_Diesel_Automatic_3.0.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Family_Carriages%2C_series_1_MET_MM53703.jpg/250px-Family_Carriages%2C_series_1_MET_MM53703.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Family_Carriages%2C_series_1_MET_MM53703.jpg/500px-Family_Carriages%2C_series_1_MET_MM53703.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb